<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leo Tolstoy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tolstoy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo Tolstoy was a Russian novelist and moral thinker of the nineteenth century, author of War and Peace and Anna Karenina. He is regarded as one of the greatest writers in world literature. His work is among the cultural achievements of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> noted in its profile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leo-tolstoy.jpg" alt="Leo Tolstoy" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergei Prokudin-Gorskii · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leo_Tolstoy_1908_Portrait_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
